{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CGTPBosuYXqUb6JtmeXbHH","type":"tool_result","content":"=== defaults/main.yml ===\n---\ncertbot_domains: []\ncertbot_email: admin@example.com\ncertbot_renew_hour: 3\n\n=== tasks/main.yml ===\n---\n- name: Install certbot\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: certbot\n    state: present\n\n- shell: certbot certificates | grep -c \"VALID\"\n  register: certbot_valid_count\n\n- name: Request a certificate for each domain\n  ansible.builtin.command: certbot certonly --standalone -d {{ item }} -m {{ certbot_email }} --agree-tos -n\n  loop: \"{{ certbot_domains }}\"\n  notify: Reload nginx\n\n- name: Write the renewal timer\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    content: |\n      [Unit]\n      Description=Renew certificates\n      [Timer]\n      OnCalendar=*-*-* {{ certbot_renew_hour }}:00:00\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/certbot-renew.timer\n\n=== README.md ===\n# certbot_renewal\n\nRequests and renews Let's Encrypt certificates.\n\n## Role variables\n\n| Variable | Default | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|---------|\n| `certbot_domains` | `[]` | Domains to request certificates for. |\n| `certbot_email` | `admin@example.com` | Registration contact address. |\n| `certbot_renew_hour` | `3` | Hour the renewal timer fires. |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41d8e4d5-fd76-410a-b295-693ca066fdef","uuid":"d9762800-7c82-4dd3-bbaf-330e66e73455","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:14:07.616Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== defaults/main.yml ===\n---\ncertbot_domains: []\ncertbot_email: admin@example.com\ncertbot_renew_hour: 3\n\n=== tasks/main.yml ===\n---\n- name: Install certbot\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: certbot\n    state: present\n\n- shell: certbot certificates | grep -c \"VALID\"\n  register: certbot_valid_count\n\n- name: Request a certificate for each domain\n  ansible.builtin.command: certbot certonly --standalone -d {{ item }} -m {{ certbot_email }} --agree-tos -n\n  l